# * aregister --chart and svg output: charts of an account's balance over time

<
2024-01-01
    assets:bank       100
    revenues:salary

2024-01-05
    expenses:food      30
    assets:bank

2024-02-01
    assets:bank       100
    revenues:salary

2024-02-10
    expenses:rent      80
    assets:bank

# ** 1. The chart data is the balance after each transaction, as a line, by date.
$ hledger -f - areg bank --chart -O csv
"commodity","series","role","mark","x","value"
"","assets:bank","item","line","2024-01-01","100"
"","assets:bank","item","line","2024-01-05","70"
"","assets:bank","item","line","2024-02-01","170"
"","assets:bank","item","line","2024-02-10","90"

# ** 2. A text chart has a row per transaction.
$ hledger -f - areg bank --chart -w 40
Transactions in assets:bank and subaccounts:

2024-01-01  100  █████████████▌
2024-01-05   70  █████████▌
2024-02-01  170  ███████████████████████
2024-02-10   90  ████████████▏

# ** 3. In SVG, the balance is a step line on a time scale.
# The expected output is in aregister-charts.svg.
$ hledger -f - areg bank -O svg | diff - aregister-charts.svg
